  "player_text": "I step out of the crush and read the notice board from top to bottom—the new taxes, the curfew, and the warning about the missing patrol.",
  "visible_motivation": "The board is posted right at the choke point with rules and a patrol warning I can use before I deal with the guards.",
  "intended_meaning": "I want the posted rules and whatever the patrol notice actually says so I know what the gate will enforce.",
  "generation_attempt_1": "You step aside from the jostling crowd to inspect the notice board carefully. The upper section details new taxes imposed by the Ash Compact authorities—the levies on trade goods, livestock, and caravan tolls have increased notably, a strain on merchants and travelers alike. Beneath that, the curfew is outlined: from dusk till dawn, movement within the gate district is restricted, enforced strictly amid rising unrest. The starkest message is the warning posted at the bottom, cautioning about a missing patrol of Cinderwatch guards last seen heading northwest along a muddy track near the stacked crates. Local rumors hint that this patrol may have fallen victim to bandits or worse, though no confirmation has surfaced. The gate serjeant nearby keeps a watchful eye on a roster, his expression hardened by the weight of these worries.",
